## A Board Meeting Is Not a Conference

A conference needs sound and a screen that reach a large room, plus breakout sessions running in parallel. A board meeting, client meeting or investor panel needs the opposite: a boardroom or hotel suite, a fixed speaker position at the head of the table, and a small group. If your event actually is a full conference with breakout rooms, see our guide to [audio visual rental for conferences](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-conferences/).

Our [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) is built for this: a gooseneck microphone for the boardroom, a 3000 lumen projector and 2x2m screen, up to 40 guests. A technician is available as an add on, not included by default, since most board meetings do not need one on site.

<InlineCTA />

## When to Step Up to the MICE Pack

For a larger corporate meeting, up to 120 guests, our [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers a 60 inch LED display, a gooseneck and wireless microphone, and a technician included on site for up to six hours. This suits an all-hands meeting or a larger investor presentation better than the boardroom-scale Basic MICE Pack.

## What We Provide, and What We Don't

We provide a gooseneck microphone, a projector or LED display, a screen, and PA sound. We do not provide video conferencing hardware, a control system, or an LED video wall: the MICE Pack's screen is a single 60 inch LED display, not a modular wall.

